 "result": "[billing-service#Data] (score 0.58)\nBillingService: Data\nBillingService stores invoices in the billing Postgres database. Invoice numbers are sequential per region and are never reused, even for voided invoices.\n\n[reporting-service#Integrations] (score 0.57)\nReportingService: Integrations\nIt depends on BillingService for invoice totals and on OrderService for order status.\n\nIts dashboards also show PaymentsService decline rates, which finance copies in by hand from the provider portal each week.\n\n[audit-service#Operations] (score 0.53)\nAuditService: Operations\nWrites are buffered for up to five seconds and flushed in batches. If a flush fails, the buffer is retried with exponential backoff until it succeeds, and the service stops accepting new events after ten minutes of failed flushes, so an outage is visible rather than silent."
}"}

